{%- comment -%}
  Under a paginated grid: a button that brings in the next page of dolls without leaving the
  page, and how many are shown of how many. Without JavaScript the button is a plain link to
  the next page, so it still works. Nothing shows on the last page.
  Accepts:
  - paginate: {Object} the paginate object
  - shown: {Number} how many items are shown up to the end of this page
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if paginate.next -%}
  <div class="load-more" data-load-more>
    <a class="button" href="{{ paginate.next.url }}" data-load-more-link data-text-loading="{{ 'collections.loading' | t }}">
      {{- 'collections.load_more' | t -}}
    </a>
    <p class="load-more__count" aria-live="polite">{{ 'collections.shown' | t: shown: shown, total: paginate.items }}</p>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
